   $q$How do the two central ideas in the final sentence relate to each other?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Users invent tools on their own, and builders later copy those tools for profit.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Cooperation between builders and users produces better tools, and those tools in turn transform the activity they serve.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Builders and users often disagree, and these disagreements usually prevent new tools from being adopted.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Better tools matter only for comfort, while the rules of a sport determine how it is played.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Cooperation between builders and users produces better tools, and those tools in turn transform the activity they serve.$q$, $q$The final sentence links cooperation (the source of good equipment) to its result (reshaping the activity), echoing paragraphs 2 through 4. Paragraph 4 says the improvements "did more than make players comfortable," which rules out the comfort-only choice.$q$, 'draft', '466576c1-bad1-576d-8384-9b3c0b9d2894')
