   $q$What does the sentence "It was not six yet" most strongly suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Someone was ringing the bell early on purpose to guide the boat.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The crew had lost track of time while waiting in the fog.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The bell was ringing from another boathouse on the lake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The groundskeeper had misread his watch and rung the bell early.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Someone was ringing the bell early on purpose to guide the boat.$q$, $q$The bell normally rings at six, so an early, steady ringing during the fog points to a deliberate signal, and the groundskeeper is later found holding a phone. Imani recognizes "a sound she knew," so it is their own boathouse bell.$q$, 'draft', '730fe2b5-2ffd-5f0f-bd80-34f061e7e099')
