   $q$What is the effect of the phrase "though its findings are less tidy than either camp might hope" at the end of paragraph 1?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It warns readers that the study was poorly designed and its data are unreliable.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It signals that the passage will now argue against both styles of training.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It reveals that the steady group clearly won on every measure in the study.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It prepares readers for mixed results rather than a clear winner.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It prepares readers for mixed results rather than a clear winner.$q$, $q$The phrase hints that neither side will be fully confirmed, and paragraph 3 delivers exactly that: a tie, a win for intervals and a win for steady work. Nothing suggests the study was poorly designed.$q$, 'draft', '51bc837d-fabf-5271-8c35-7d7749629811')
