   $q$Why does the author end paragraph 1 by asking whether the colors were "gone or merely hidden"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To suggest that the records about the curtain's colors were probably wrong.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To show that the author has no interest in how the question is answered.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"To create suspense that the next paragraph resolves, pulling the reader forward.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To explain the method Kobayashi used to clean the whole curtain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-paragraphs"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To create suspense that the next paragraph resolves, pulling the reader forward.$q$, $q$The open question leads directly into the test in paragraph 2, where the blue sky appears and answers it. The cleaning method for the whole curtain comes later, in paragraph 3.$q$, 'draft', 'e13bfab3-c982-5ce4-9253-9488b16c5297')
