   $q$In "vitality," the root vit means "life." Which word below contains the same root with a related meaning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"evidence","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sound-alike-root"},{"text":"visibility","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sound-alike-root"},{"text":"revitalize","is_correct":true},{"text":"invitation","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"spelling-coincidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$revitalize$q$, $q$Revitalize means to give new life to something, so it shares the root vit and its meaning of life, just as the bay's vitality is its lively health. Invitation contains the letters v, i, t, but it comes from a word meaning to ask, not from the root for life.$q$, 'draft', 'e3c23a21-e91e-5e9a-bdfa-606154d2af13')
