   $q$The prefix poly- means "many," and phon means "sound" or "voice." What are "polyphonic" pieces?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Music that uses a single melody repeated many times","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Music that is too complicated for any audience to enjoy","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Music in which several melodies are heard at the same time","is_correct":true},{"text":"Music written for many concerts over many years","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Music in which several melodies are heard at the same time$q$, $q$Poly plus phon means many voices, and the passage says "several independent melodies wove around one another." A single repeated melody ignores the "many" voices sounding together.$q$, 'draft', 'ee47fb45-ac2b-5a47-a651-efdc0d8c5d75')
