values
  ('9c7f8159-1323-5e3c-87f5-98bf414a2344', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$"Euphoria" begins with the same prefix as "euphonious." Based on that prefix, what was the reporter asking Marisol when he mentioned "euphoria"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Whether she had heard pleasing sounds in the hall","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overextends-shared-root"},{"text":"Whether she had felt relief that the work was over","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-answer-with-question"},{"text":"Whether she had felt an intense rush of happiness","is_correct":true},{"text":"Whether she had felt nervous before the audience","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Whether she had felt an intense rush of happiness$q$, $q$The prefix eu- means "good," and euphoria names a strong feeling of joy, which is what the reporter expected. Relief is Marisol's answer, chosen in contrast to euphoria, so it is not what the question asked.$q$, 'draft', 'ee47fb45-ac2b-5a47-a651-efdc0d8c5d75')
