  ('0aaaafec-133a-5c6b-9754-e64a8974cb54', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g12-word-parts'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The prefix re- means "again," and gen means "to produce" or "to create." What does the axolotl do when it can "regenerate" lost body parts?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It protects its body from losing parts","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"It grows the missing parts back again","is_correct":true},{"text":"It produces young that have extra limbs","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-first-root"},{"text":"It replaces the parts with scar tissue","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It grows the missing parts back again$q$, $q$Re plus gen means to produce again, and the passage says "a complete, working limb eventually grows back." Scar tissue is what human bodies usually form instead, which the passage contrasts with regeneration.$q$, 'draft', '9a26d17e-2591-5be8-b3e2-5287ae4ca605')
