   $q$The root omni means "all," vor means "to eat," and -ous means "having the quality of." What does it mean that many feeder visitors are "omnivorous"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They eat many kinds of food, both plant and animal","is_correct":true},{"text":"They eat only seeds throughout the year","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"They eat at every feeder in the neighborhood","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misapplies-root"},{"text":"They eat only during the coldest months","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They eat many kinds of food, both plant and animal$q$, $q$Omni plus vor means eating all kinds of things, and the passage lists "insects, spiders, berries, and seeds." Eating only seeds is too narrow, since seeds become essential only when insects are scarce.$q$, 'draft', '0d56c0a4-d8a4-525e-bc7d-64be0afa701d')
