insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('ba3907b4-7ff2-5129-87ff-c9384d617438', 'wg4-informative-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g4-informative-writing'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Power from the Wind$q$, $q$(1) Wind turbines are tall machines that turn wind into electricity. (2) You may have seen rows of them standing on hills or out in the ocean. (3) Each one looks a bit like a giant pinwheel.

(4) A turbine has three main parts. (5) The tower holds everything high in the air, where the wind is stronger. (6) The blades catch the wind and spin around. (7) The blades are connected to a machine called a generator. (8) When the blades spin, the generator makes electricity.

(9) Wind power has some good points. (10) Wind will never run out. (11) Turbines also do not make smoke that dirties the air. (12) Still, turbines only work well in places with steady wind. (13) My favorite kind of weather is a warm, sunny day.$q$, 'draft')
