insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('94d4c409-cdd7-5645-89fc-d4ad6ae5f7a2', 'wg4-informative-writing-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g4-informative-writing'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Sea Turtle Hatchlings$q$, $q$(1) Sea turtles spend almost their whole lives in the ocean. (2) However, they begin their lives on land.

(3) A mother sea turtle crawls onto a sandy beach at night. (4) She digs a deep hole with her back flippers. (5) She lays about one hundred eggs, which are round and soft. (6) Then she covers the nest with sand and returns to the sea.

(7) The eggs stay buried for about two months. (8) The warm sand keeps them at the right temperature. (9) Then the baby turtles, called hatchlings, break out of their shells. (10) They dig up to the surface together. (11) Hatchlings usually come out at night when the sand is cooler. (12) They crawl toward the brightest horizon, which is often the ocean.

(13) Beach lights can confuse hatchlings. (14) Some towns ask people to turn off outdoor lights during nesting season.$q$, 'draft')
