        '3-5', $q$Walk to School Day$q$, $q$(1) Many students at Brookside School ride in cars, even when they live only a few blocks away. (2) ______ (3) First, walking is healthy. (4) Doctors say children need about an hour of exercise every day, and a walk to school is a good start.

(5) Second, fewer cars would make the air cleaner around our school. (6) In order to keep everyone safe, parent helpers could stand at each corner on walk days. (7) Walking also gives friends time to talk before class. (8) Students who walk together often arrive at school laughing and in a good mood.$q$, 'draft')
