        '3-5', $q$How a Butterfly Grows$q$, $q$(1) A butterfly goes through four stages as it grows. (2) First, a female butterfly lays tiny eggs on a leaf. (3) After a few days, a small caterpillar hatches from each egg. (4) The caterpillar eats and eats, and it grows bigger every day. (5) ____, it hangs upside down and forms a hard shell called a chrysalis. (6) Inside the chrysalis, its body slowly changes. (7) Finally, an adult butterfly pushes its way out and spreads its wings.

(8) Butterflies help plants in an important way. (9) When a butterfly drinks nectar from a flower, a yellow dust called pollen sticks to its legs. (10) Then the butterfly carries the pollen to the next flower. (11) This helps the flowers make seeds. (12) Moths usually fly at night instead of during the day. (13) Because of butterflies, gardens and fields can keep growing year after year.$q$, 'draft')
