        '3-5', $q$The First Bicycles$q$, $q$(1) Bicycles did not always look the way they do today. (2) More than two hundred years ago, the first bicycle-like machine was made of wood. (3) It had no pedals at all. (4) Instead, riders pushed their feet against the ground to roll forward. (5) Later, inventors added pedals to the front wheel. (6) ____, riding was still bumpy because the wheels were made of wood or iron.

(7) Some later bicycles had a giant front wheel and a tiny back wheel. (8) These bikes went fast, but riders often fell off the high seat. (9) Then builders made a safer bicycle with two wheels of the same size. (10) Rubber tires filled with air made the ride smooth. (11) My bike is blue and has a shiny bell on it. (12) Step by step, the bicycle became the safe and simple machine we ride today.$q$, 'draft')
