  ('f6267eb2-754e-5f0d-b78b-2d323ac214c4', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g4-precise-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the sentence: "Inside the old trunk, Nadia found her grandmother's first painting." Which revision best uses punctuation to build up to the surprise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Inside the old trunk? Nadia found her grandmother's first painting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-end-mark"},{"text":"Inside the old trunk, Nadia found her grandmother's first painting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-change"},{"text":"Inside the old trunk, Nadia found... her grandmother's first painting!","is_correct":true},{"text":"Inside, the old trunk, Nadia found, her grandmother's, first painting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-error"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Inside the old trunk, Nadia found... her grandmother's first painting!$q$, $q$The ellipsis makes the reader wait a moment, and the exclamation point shows the surprise when the painting is revealed. Adding many commas creates pauses, but they break the sentence apart in the wrong places.$q$, 'draft', null)
